            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0329" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/3285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-02T17:00:00+01:00">July 2, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 2—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. While complete information still lacking here regarding events Germany
                    following observations may be made: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Noticeable decrease bombing outrages.</item>
                        <pb facs="0330" n="230" xml:id="pg230"/>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Austrian frontier guarded against influx fleeing National
                            Socialists.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Government feels policies regarding Nazis and Germany vindicated by
                            events and Chancellor has declared stronger action will be taken against
                            terrorists.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Developments Germany real blow to Austrian Nazi movement.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>Austrian press generally opinion that National Socialism and Hitler
                            both have lost tremendously in prestige.</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>Position Chancellor and Government in my opinion much
                            strengthened.</item>
                        <label>7.</label>
                        <item>Situation here entirely quiet.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
